course: dictionary
lesson: 12744
title: Describing words with drunken
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drunken is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you about a noun. It means drunk, or often drunk, and drunk means affected by too much alcohol. «The drunken shouting woke the whole street.» The context tells you the shouting was loud, and the word drunken tells you it came from people who had drunk too much alcohol.
explain: Drunken also goes with other words, such as «drunken behaviour» and «drunken singing». Behaviour means the way someone acts, so drunken behaviour is the way someone acts when they are drunk. Health lessons link these actions with the dangers of alcohol, because drinking too much can make people act in unsafe ways.
explain: Sometimes drunken describes things, not people. The meaning is swaying or crooked, as if something were drunk. «The old fence stood at a drunken angle after the storm.» The fence is not drunk. It leans and sways as if it had had too much to drink. The context helps you see that.
fact: Drunken means drunk, or often drunk, affected by too much alcohol.
fact: «Drunken behaviour» means the way people act when they are drunk.
fact: «Drunken singing» is loud, messy singing by people who are drunk.
fact: The old sea song «What shall we do with the drunken sailor?» uses this word.
fact: Drunken can describe something that sways or leans crooked, as in «a drunken sailor» swaying along the deck.
exercise: What does drunken tell us about the shouting in «The drunken shouting woke the whole street.»? | *It was made by people who were drunk | It was very quiet and gentle | It was made by a choir singing carols | It was made in a library
exercise: «The drunken sailor swayed along the harbour.» What does swayed mean? | *Moved unsteadily from side to side | Stood perfectly still | Ran very fast | Fell asleep at once
exercise: Meera says drunken means very sleepy. What is the right meaning? | Early in the morning | Very cheerful and full of fun | Very sleepy and yawning | *Drunk, or often drunk, affected by too much alcohol
test: Health lessons teach that drunken behaviour is linked with the dangers of which substance? | *Alcohol | Sunshine | Sugar | Sleep
test: «The fence leaned at a drunken angle after the storm.» What does drunken mean here? | *Swaying or crooked, as if drunk | Full of cheer and fun | Painted bright blue | Fast and noisy
exam: Which phrase means noisy singing by people who have drunk too much alcohol? | barely a whisper | *drunken singing | ancient humming | glum silence
